Create Amazon ECR (Elastic Container Registry) Repository

1. Login to AWS Console.

2. Search for "Amazon ECR".

3. Click "Private repositories".

4. Click "Create repository".

5. Configure the repository:
   - Visibility: Private
   - Repository name: bankingwebapp (Must match IMAGE_NAME in Jenkinsfile)
   - Tag immutability: Mutable (Default)
   - Encryption: AES-256 (Default)
   - Scan on push: Optional (Enable if required)

6. Click "Create repository".

7. Copy the Repository URI. It should look like:
   <AWS_ACCOUNT_ID>.dkr.ecr.<AWS_REGION>.amazonaws.com/bankingwebapp

8. Verify from the Jenkins server:
   aws ecr describe-repositories --region ap-south-1

9. Ensure the Jenkins EC2 IAM Role has the following permission:
   AmazonEC2ContainerRegistryPowerUser

Example:

Repository Name:
bankingwebapp

Repository URI:
123456789012.dkr.ecr.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/bankingwebapp

Note:
- Create the ECR repository only once.
- Repository name must match IMAGE_NAME in your Jenkinsfile.
- Every pipeline execution will push a new image tag (1, 2, 3, ...) into the same repository.
